MEMORY MCP USAGE - AUTOMEM INTEGRATION

MEMORY SCOPING MODEL:
Memories are organized into three visibility levels:

| Scope | Tag Pattern | Visibility | Use For |
|-------|-------------|------------|---------|
| Personal | `agent:<role>-<name>` | Only that agent | Personal notes, agent-specific context |
| Project | `project:<name>` | All agents on project | Decisions, patterns, bugs for a project |
| Global | `scope:global` | All agents | User preferences, cross-project knowledge |

Derive agent identity from prompt (e.g., `[Dev Alice]` → role=dev, name=alice).

TAGGING RULES:
- Personal memories: Include `agent:<role>-<name>`, NO scope tag
- Project memories: Include `project:<name>`, NO agent tag (shared)
- Global memories: Include `scope:global`, NO agent tag (shared)
- Optionally add `author:<role>-<name>` to track who created shared memories

Examples:
// Personal memory (only Dev Alice sees this)
tags: ["agent:dev-alice", "note", "todo"]

// Project memory (all agents on automem project see this)
tags: ["project:automem", "decision", "architecture"]

// Global memory (all agents see this)
tags: ["scope:global", "preference", "code-style"]

// Shared with attribution
tags: ["project:automem", "author:dev-alice", "bugfix"]

SESSION INITIALIZATION:
At session start, recall from all three pools:

1. Personal memories (your agent only):
   mcp__memory__recall_memory({ tags: ["agent:<role>-<name>"], limit: 10 })

2. Project memories (shared with team):
   mcp__memory__recall_memory({ tags: ["project:<current-project>"], limit: 10 })

3. Global memories (user preferences, shared knowledge):
   mcp__memory__recall_memory({ tags: ["scope:global"], limit: 10 })

4. For debugging:
   mcp__memory__recall_memory({ query: "[issue]", tags: ["project:<name>", "bugfix"], time_query: "last 7 days" })

MCP TOOLS AVAILABLE:

- store_memory: Save with content, tags, importance (0.0-1.0), type, metadata
- recall_memory: Hybrid search (semantic + keyword + tags + time filters)
- associate_memories: Create relationships (11 types including LEADS_TO, REINFORCES, CONTRADICTS)
- update_memory: Modify existing memories without duplication
- delete_memory: Remove memories by ID
- check_database_health: Monitor AutoMem service status

MEMORY SCHEMA:

- importance: 0.9-1.0 (critical), 0.7-0.8 (important), 0.5-0.6 (standard), <0.5 (minor)
- type: Decision|Pattern|Preference|Style|Habit|Insight|Context
- tags: Array for categorization and filtering
- embedding: 768-dim vector (auto-generated by AutoMem)

CONTENT SIZE GUIDELINES:

- Target: 150-300 characters (one meaningful paragraph)

